From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: fix H616 PLL audio SDM rates

The H616 PLL audio clock has a fixed post-divider of two. The NM clock
implementation multiplies the requested observable clock rate by this
divider before looking it up in the sigma-delta modulation table, and
divides the table rate by two again when recalculating the observable
rate.

Store the corresponding VCO rates in the SDM table so requests for the
90.3168 MHz and 98.304 MHz output rates select their exact SDM settings.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-h616.c
@@ -223,8 +223,8 @@ static const struct clk_parent_data pll_periph0_2x_parents[] = {
  * frequencies with less error.
  */
 static struct ccu_sdm_setting pll_audio_sdm_table[] = {
-	{ .rate = 90316800, .pattern = 0xc001288d, .m = 3, .n = 22 },
-	{ .rate = 98304000, .pattern = 0xc001eb85, .m = 5, .n = 40 },
+	{ .rate = 180633600, .pattern = 0xc001288d, .m = 3, .n = 22 },
+	{ .rate = 196608000, .pattern = 0xc001eb85, .m = 5, .n = 40 },
 };
 
 #define SUN50I_H616_PLL_AUDIO_REG	0x078
-- 
2.47.3
